WEBVTT

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:06.700
This is a pile of sheets full of counts. In about a minute it's going to write a sentence that nobody has ever written.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:20.180
Each row is a word from a book, and the words that came next, with a mark every time. Maybe you did the counting yourselves; maybe the sheets arrived finished. It works the same either way.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:34.980
Every box has a colour, always in the same order: red, blue, green, yellow. On this row, red means "magpie". On another row, red means something else.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:49.880
A story starts after a full stop, so find the row for full stop. Fill a cup with one counter for every mark: seven red for "it", four blue for "here", three green, three yellow.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:01:02.820
Seventeen counters. Now draw one without looking. Red: "it". Write the word down, tip the cup back, and go to the row for "it".

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:11.760
The row for "it": three red, three blue, three green, one yellow. Red again: "sits".

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:19.300
"Sits" is only ever followed by "on", and "on" by "the". One box, no cup.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:35.500
The row for "the" fills the cup with all four colours. Yellow: "dog". And after "dog", two red for a full stop, two blue for "runs". Red: full stop.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:44.980
"It sits on the dog." The book never says that; the magpie sits on the fence. Nobody wrote this sentence; the counting did.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.920
And here's everything this model could have written instead.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.900
Every draw picks a different path. So run it ten thousand times and count what comes out.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:08.540
Every story different. Every story sounding like the book. That's what Claude or ChatGPT is doing every time it writes a word, with vastly more counts than this.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:25.640
Four jobs in your group. A reader finds the row. A filler puts one counter per mark in the cup. A drawer pulls one out. And a writer writes the word down. Tip the cup back every time.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:30.980
Reader, find the full stop. Let's see what your book says.
